(6146470, 904841, 114682, '<td valign="top">Thank you so much for your votes and comments, it''s my personal best and first top 10!!<br/>The place is called Kvarnbyn, it''s located in Möldnal, a town which was historically independent, but with time it grew and is now connected to Gothenburg, Sweden. It consist''s of a system of several watermills which were before used in different industries, now it''s more of a tourist attraction as more or less all industries were transferred elsewhere. It''s really nice there, but the strangest thing was that I didn''t think at all about it fot the Rusty challenge, before I walked with my 7 months old son there the last day of entry submission. I suddenly was struck by the scene and I knew that I just must compete. I invested otherwise a lot of planning in my Yellow challenge, which ended more or less in fiasco, and for the Rusty challenge I just took couple of shots without any preparation at all and it turned to be my PB.<br/>Such is life!</td>', 'Thank you so much for your votes and comments, it''s my personal best and first top 10!!The place is called Kvarnbyn, it''s located in Möldnal, a town which was historically independent, but with time it grew and is now connected to Gothenburg, Sweden. It consist''s of a system of several watermills which were before used in different industries, now it''s more of a tourist attraction as more or less all industries were transferred elsewhere. It''s really nice there, but the strangest thing was that I didn''t think at all about it fot the Rusty challenge, before I walked with my 7 months old son there the last day of entry submission. I suddenly was struck by the scene and I knew that I just must compete. I invested otherwise a lot of planning in my Yellow challenge, which ended more or less in fiasco, and for the Rusty challenge I just took couple of shots without any preparation at all and it turned to be my PB.Such is life!', '2010-08-31 07:41:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6146513, 904832, 103142, '<td valign="top">I couldn''t make up my mind about the background. The land in the distance added to part of the story, yet it kept drawing my eye, and I didn''t find a lot of interest once it settled there. I gave it a 6, but I think it would have been a 7 with a tighter crop. There''s already so much to peruse--the rope, the bird, the rust, the shapes, and I think that land added on too many things and split the interest. <br/> <br/>Your outtake, while nice, doesn''t have the interest of the dragger''s drum, imo. (maybe because there''s a bird in it :)</td>', 'I couldn''t make up my mind about the background. The land in the distance added to part of the story, yet it kept drawing my eye, and I didn''t find a lot of interest once it settled there. I gave it a 6, but I think it would have been a 7 with a tighter crop. There''s already so much to peruse--the rope, the bird, the rust, the shapes, and I think that land added on too many things and split the interest.  Your outtake, while nice, doesn''t have the interest of the dragger''s drum, imo. (maybe because there''s a bird in it :)', '2010-08-31 10:01:55.000000', NULL, 0),
